<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Windbreak Grant Application</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/app.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <div class="page">
    <header class="topbar">
      <div class="topbar-inner">
        <div>
          <span class="topbar-brand">Land &amp; Nature Agency</span>
          <span class="topbar-title">Windbreak Grant Scheme</span>
        </div>
        <div class="topbar-session">
          <span class="muted-inverse">Government portal session</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="container">
      <ol class="stepper" aria-label="Application steps">
        <li class="active"><span class="step-no">1</span> Your details</li>
        <li><span class="step-no">2</span> Draw windbreak</li>
        <li><span class="step-no">3</span> Review</li>
        <li><span class="step-no">4</span> Submitted</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="card card-center">
        <h1>Apply for a grant to plant a windbreak</h1>
        <p>
          A windbreak protects crops and livestock and improves nature on
          your farm. In this prototype you are <strong>already signed in</strong>
          to the government portal, so the service looks up your details and
          your registered land automatically.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          The only thing you have to provide is <strong>where</strong> you
          want the windbreak: draw the lines on the map of your land and
          submit.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-large" href="/apply">Apply for windbreak</a>
        <p class="muted small">
          Assumed session identity: <code>{{demoFullName}}</code> &middot;
          kennitala <code>{{demoKennitala}}</code> (set via DEMO_FULL_NAME /
          DEMO_KENNITALA)
        </p>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer class="app-footer">
      <div class="container">
        <p>
          Prototype &mdash; farmer authentication is assumed to have happened
          in the portal. Data is served by a pygeoapi OGC API and stored in
          local GeoJSON files.
        </p>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
